One day you're researching how humans explore vast search spaces through an obscure system called Picbreeder. Then, almost 20 years later, Picbreeder images are going on display at a major art world event in Venice. It's hard to believe! This is a good opportunity to credit the full founding Picbreeder team who worked with me on this project, starting with the man who had the original idea to make a crowd-sourced image breeding site, @jsecretan: Jimmy Secretan, Nick Beato, David D'Ambrosio, Adam Campbell, and Adelein Rodriguez. Great work team, almost 20 years later still achieving unexpected things!

Thanks also to @matdryhurst for seeing something deeper in Picbreeder than just a bunch of old genetic art.

@matdryhurst: "Strange Rules opens May 4th @ Palazzo Diedo Venice. Curated with @HUObrist, @hollyherndon, and Adriana Rispoli. Opening 7pm, all are welcome."
